From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] inetcomm: IMimeMessage persistence and properties, IMimeAllocator frees (2047)

inetcomm: IMimeMessage persistence and properties, and the IMimeAllocator frees.

Save writes the text a message was loaded from while nothing changed and
rebuilds it from its bodies (multipart parts between boundary lines) once a
body is dirty; IsDirty, GetSizeMax, GetMessageSize, GetMessageSource,
GetFlags (IMF_*), GetClassID, InitNew, SaveBody and GetBodyOffsets work.
GetProp/SetProp/DeleteProp/QueryProp act on the root body and
QueryBodyProp/SetBodyProp/DeleteBodyProp on a given body. The allocator's
GetSize, DidAlloc, HeapMinimize, FreeAddressList/Props, ReleaseObjects,
FreeEnumHeaderRowArray, FreeEnumPropertyArray, FreeThumbprint and
PropVariantClear free what they say. They were stubs.
